---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Keep this in step with the Play Console Data Safety form — reviewers compare
// the two, and a mismatch is a rejection.
const updated = "13 August 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — LetsMock"
  description="What LetsMock records during a mock interview, who processes it, how long it is kept, and how to delete it."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink-50">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-400">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 space-y-10 leading-relaxed [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-ink-50 [&_p]:mt-3 [&_p]:text-ink-400 [&_li]:mt-2 [&_li]:text-ink-400 [&_ul]:mt-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_a]:text-ember-400 [&_a]:underline"
    >
      <section
        class="rounded-2xl border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900 p-6 [&_p]:text-ink-200"
      >
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          LetsMock does not ask you to create an account. We do not collect your
          name, email address or phone number. To run an interview we process
          your <strong class="text-ink-50">voice</strong>, and — if you choose to
          upload one — the text of your <strong class="text-ink-50">resume</strong
          >. You can delete everything at any time by emailing us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Your voice during an interview.</strong>
            Audio is streamed while a mock interview is in progress so the app can
            transcribe what you say and reply to it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">The transcript of the interview.</strong>
            Text of both sides of the conversation, with timings, so we can score
            your answers and show you the transcript afterwards.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Your resume, if you upload one.</strong>
            We extract the plain text from the PDF so the interviewer can ask about
            your actual projects. We do not keep the original file.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Your scorecard.</strong> The scores, feedback
            and speech metrics generated after each interview.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">An anonymous app identifier.</strong> A random
            id generated on your device to keep track of your interviews and whether
            you have an active subscription. It is not linked to your identity.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do <strong class="text-ink-50">not</strong> collect your name, email
          address, phone number, contacts, photos, location or advertising identifiers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Why we process it</h2>
        <p>
          Solely to provide the app: to conduct the interview, generate your
          scorecard, show you your history, and apply your free-tier or
          subscription entitlement. We do not sell your data, and we do not use
          your interviews for advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Who processes it for us</h2>
        <p>
          A mock interview is not possible without sending audio and text to
          specialist services. Each one processes data only to deliver its part
          of the service:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">LiveKit</strong> — carries the live audio
            between your device and our interviewer, and stores session recordings
            and transcripts that we use to diagnose faults.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Deepgram</strong> — converts your speech to
            text, and generates the interviewer's voice.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Groq</strong> — runs the language model that
            decides what to ask next and writes your scorecard.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">RevenueCat</strong> — manages subscriptions
            and receipts. It receives the anonymous app identifier, never your interview
            content.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Google Play</strong> — processes payments.
            We never see or store your card details.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Transcripts and scorecards</strong> — kept
            so you can revisit past interviews and track progress, until you ask us
            to delete them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Resume text</strong> — kept until you replace
            it or ask us to delete it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink-50">Session recordings held by LiveKit</strong>
            — retained only for troubleshooting and deleted on their standard schedule.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:support@letsmock.com">support@letsmock.com</a>
          from the device you use, and we will delete your interviews, transcripts,
          scorecards and resume text. Uninstalling the app on its own does not delete
          data already stored, because there is no account for us to close.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Children</h2>
        <p>
          LetsMock is intended for people preparing for employment and is not
          directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from
          children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Security</h2>
        <p>
          Audio and API traffic are encrypted in transit. Access to stored
          interview data is limited to the operator of the service. No system is
          perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes materially we will update the date at the top of
          this page and, where the change is significant, note it in the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          LetsMock is operated by an individual developer, Biprayan Choudhuri, in
          India. Questions or data requests:
          <a href="mailto:support@letsmock.com">support@letsmock.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
